notes=1280x720 progressive using the game's own widescreen path.<br>Menus use the 640x480 layouts scaled by the game; HUD elements anchored to their screen edges (native sprite size).<br>Menu/transition Bink movies scaled to full screen; fullscreen intro movies centered at native size.<br>Only default.xbe is changed (no .vpp edits).<br><br>Enable 720p in the dashboard, component/HDMI out, REQUIRES 128MB RAM.<br><br>Temporarily lifts the Cerbios 3.1.0 kernel's 64MB contiguous-memory limit while the game reserves its startup pools, then restores it before graphics init (does nothing on other BIOSes).
#XBE init flags 0x80000005->0x80000001: clear 'limit to 64MB' so a 128MB console gives the game the extra RAM 720p needs
0x00000124:01000080
#Header size 0x105C->0x1400 so the loader also maps the unused bytes after the header (used for the code caves below)
0x00000108:00140000
#Kernel fix 1/4 (code in header slack, VA 0x11060): if this is Cerbios 3.1.0 (mov ecx,3FDFh at 0x8002255E), raise MmAllocateContiguousMemoryEx's limit to 0x7FDF (128MB) so the game's ~34MB of startup pools land in the upper 64MB
0x00001060:9C60FABE5E250280803EB97520817E01DF3F000075170F20C089C325FFFFFEFF0F22C0C74601DF7F00000F22C3619D8B0D18010100E9D09E1B00
#Kernel fix 2/4: entry point (VA 0x1CAF64) runs the code above before the CRT allocates its pools
0x001BAF64:E9F760E4FF90
#Kernel fix 3/4 (header slack VA 0x110A0): put Cerbios' 64MB limit back (7FDF -> 3FDF) before the D3D device is created, so framebuffers stay below 64MB (IGRDash and screenshots keep working)
0x000010A0:9C60FABE5E250280803EB97520817E01DF7F000075170F20C089C325FFFFFEFF0F22C0C74601DF3F00000F22C3619D83EC4453BB01000000E93CEC1500
